1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,810
Loopback Transformer:

2
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:05,510
Towards a Unified View of
Residual Looped Transformers.

3
00:00:07,310 --> 00:00:09,820
Linear attention keeps a running memory:

4
00:00:10,170 --> 00:00:13,120
each token adds its key
and value to a state,

5
00:00:13,410 --> 00:00:15,320
and later tokens read it.

6
00:00:15,630 --> 00:00:18,600
A residual stream does
the same across layers:

7
00:00:19,130 --> 00:00:21,580
each block adds its update to the stream,

8
00:00:21,930 --> 00:00:24,040
and the next block reads the sum.

9
00:00:24,790 --> 00:00:26,360
Layers play the role of tokens,

10
00:00:26,930 --> 00:00:29,220
and the stream plays
the role of the state.

11
00:00:31,390 --> 00:00:32,240
In this view,

12
00:00:32,290 --> 00:00:34,700
every residual rule sets three things:

13
00:00:34,830 --> 00:00:35,960
the input's strength,

14
00:00:36,450 --> 00:00:37,900
the total weight of the updates,

15
00:00:38,230 --> 00:00:39,760
and how that weight is shared.

16
00:00:40,430 --> 00:00:41,920
When the same blocks repeat,

17
00:00:42,470 --> 00:00:44,920
plain addition lets the
total grow with every pass.

18
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,990
Loopback sets the three separately.

19
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:51,990
The input keeps weight
one on its own path,

20
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:53,690
a decay bounds the total,

21
00:00:54,040 --> 00:00:56,630
and attention shares it
across the stored updates.

22
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:01,930
Here a standard Transformer and Loopback,

23
00:01:01,930 --> 00:01:03,430
both at 3B scale,

24
00:01:03,430 --> 00:01:05,080
read the same new text.

25
00:01:05,530 --> 00:01:07,330
Loopback is 23% smaller,

26
00:01:07,330 --> 00:01:09,200
and its loss still ends lower.

27
00:01:11,130 --> 00:01:14,120
From 191M to 3B parameters,

28
00:01:14,530 --> 00:01:17,120
Loopback gets lower loss than the standard

29
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:19,860
Transformer with 40–75% of its parameters.

30
00:01:22,030 --> 00:01:24,040
Against seven other looped designs,

31
00:01:24,390 --> 00:01:26,563
it has the lowest loss and the highest

32
00:01:26,563 --> 00:01:29,400
benchmark average at all
three sizes we tested.

33
00:01:31,930 --> 00:01:33,410
And at 3B parameters,

34
00:01:33,410 --> 00:01:36,080
it more than doubles
word-problem accuracy,

35
00:01:36,250 --> 00:01:39,100
from 2.6% to 6.4%.

36
00:01:42,030 --> 00:01:43,000
That's Loopback.

37
00:01:43,310 --> 00:01:43,980
Fewer parameters,

38
00:01:44,370 --> 00:01:44,880
lower loss.

39
00:01:45,510 --> 00:01:47,280
The paper and code are
on our project page.

